                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7b9484a1-e354-3c95-bdf3-ddedbd9f178f",
                        "entry_id": "cbd159c4-08f3-39b7-813c-2913d72fe508",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. мысленно отвлекаться (отвлечься) от тех или иных сторон, свойств или связей предметов и явлений с целью выделения существенных и закономерных их признаков"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "204871c8-1375-4895-bf28-d08046f49ccd",
                                "sense_id": "7b9484a1-e354-3c95-bdf3-ddedbd9f178f",
                                "text": "Попадая на этот остров, человек абстрагируется от проблем и готов к медитации."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "22a51d4b-3377-4265-bf90-1e540cdd9b05",
                        "source_entry_id": "cbd159c4-08f3-39b7-813c-2913d72fe508",
                        "source_sense_id": "7b9484a1-e354-3c95-bdf3-ddedbd9f178f",
                        "target_lang_word": "disengage",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "disengage",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac8a0489-884d-367d-8a54-399616280a16",
                                        "entry_id": "62b164e1-c13a-364c-a3fa-75ba1fc453b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A circular movement of the blade that avoids the opponent's parry"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "disengage",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2155e324-4007-3d36-b00f-9743ce5709e1",
                                        "entry_id": "64ace8bb-f4fa-39af-ace9-10a50efea0ae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To release or loosen from something that binds, entangles, holds, or interlocks."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c94b1224-408c-4e35-981b-4b18d9c2d740",
                                                "sense_id": "2155e324-4007-3d36-b00f-9743ce5709e1",
                                                "text": "Diſingaging myſelf then from his embrace, I made him ſenſible of the reaſons there were for his preſent leaving me; on which, tho' reluctantly, he put on his cloaths with as little expedition, however, as he could help, wantonly interrupting himſelf between whiles, with kiſſes, touches, and embraces, I could not refuſe myſelf to; [...]",
                                                "translation": "Fanny Hill",
                                                "english": "Fanny Hill"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc877196-a1b5-4a9a-ad7a-e00cc2bb3e08",
                                                "sense_id": "2155e324-4007-3d36-b00f-9743ce5709e1",
                                                "text": "With the help of a sleepy waiter, Little Billee got the bacchanalian into his room and lit his candle for him, and, disengaging himself from his maudlin embraces, left him to wallow in solitude."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f86edbb-233a-4f78-a5ce-852e3d748166",
                                                "sense_id": "2155e324-4007-3d36-b00f-9743ce5709e1",
                                                "text": "The eight-cylinder Rolls-Royce diesel engines drive through \"Twin Disc\" torque converters up to a speed of some 46 m.p.h., when the drive automatically changes to direct coupling and the torque converter is disengaged."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fad0e4b-e864-4f76-aebd-8ec5933d9b94",
                                                "sense_id": "2155e324-4007-3d36-b00f-9743ce5709e1",
                                                "text": "Ford still had his hand stuck out. Arthur looked at it with incomprehension.¶ \"Shake,\" prompted Ford.¶ Arthur did, nervously at first, as if it might turn out to be a fish. Then he grasped it vigorously with both hands in an overwhelming flood of relief. He shook it and shook it.¶ After a while Ford found it necessary to disengage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b38f5d18-a9b7-4014-9fac-b93e86f8efd2",
                                                "sense_id": "2155e324-4007-3d36-b00f-9743ce5709e1",
                                                "text": "Three weeks before the election in Iraq, conversation has started bubbling up in Congress, in the Pentagon and some days even in the White House about when and how American forces might begin to disengage in Iraq."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f727ec1-03cc-48d7-be4b-3655d4e6f51d",
                                                "sense_id": "2155e324-4007-3d36-b00f-9743ce5709e1",
                                                "text": "The more established wisdom about trolls, at this point, is to disengage."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "23d477c2-d046-4c12-8639-177c0c55569a",
